     Function ddwwaarrff__nneeww__ffddee() allocates a new DWARF frame descriptor.

     Argument _d_b_g should reference a DWARF producer instance allocated using
     dwarf_producer_init(3) or dwarf_producer_init_b(3).

     If argument _e_r_r is not NULL, it will be used to store error information
     in case of an error.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     On success, function ddwwaarrff__nneeww__ffddee() returns the newly created frame de‐
     scriptor.  In case of an error, function ddwwaarrff__nneeww__ffddee() returns
     DW_DLV_BADADDR and sets the argument _e_r_r.

EERRRROORRSS
     Function ddwwaarrff__nneeww__ffddee() can fail with:

     [DW_DLE_ARGUMENT]  Argument _d_b_g was NULL.

     [DW_DLE_MEMORY]    An out of memory condition was encountered during the
                        execution of the function.

